CORE
main.cpp

^\[main\.assertion\.1\] .* allocation function template: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] .* member of a class template: SUCCESS$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Overload resolution for the allocation function ([expr.new]/20) considers
function templates, in a new-expression that is itself in a template, and
the allocation functions of a class template specialization.
